      "content": "i already tried calling them. they just give me the runaround with these scripted responses about \"system updates\" and \"standardized fees\" but the timing is way too convenient with everything else going on. calling them just feels like i'm giving them more info to use against me. they're obviously aware that i've noticed the pattern. i don't want to just file a complaint that'll get buried, i need to know how to actually protect my money from being targeted. what are some ways to move my funds or structure my accounts so they can't disrupt my access or keep hitting me with these predatory fees?",
